          "title": "You'll want to know: il diritto",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "il diritto — \"the right; law (as a subject)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Tutti hanno diritto a un avvocato. Everyone has the right to a lawyer."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Avere diritto a — to be entitled to. Studiare diritto — to study law. As an adjective it means straight."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "diritto is inherited from Vulgar Latin dērēctus, a form of Latin dīrēctus \"straight\" (EtymDB), from dīrigere \"to set straight\", built on regere \"to rule\": what is straight is what is right."
            }
          ]
        },
